ms (fever, weight loss) argue against CML-BC in favor of a de novo acute process?", "summary": ""}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of abnormal mean corpuscular volume (MCV) or bone marrow morphology in the lab results disfavor MDS-EB as a diagnosis?", "summary": ""}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or Ph chromosome detection in the vignette findings disfavor CML in blast crisis (B3.1)?", "summary": ""}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) in a patient with high leukocyte count disfavor polycythemia vera (PV) as a diagnosis?", "summary": ""}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the thrombocytopenia (109,000/mm³) contradict essential thrombocythemia (ET) in chronic/accelerated phase (B3.3) and support a different etiology?", "summary": ""}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present (airway, respiratory, haemodynamic, or neurological compromise). The patient is hemodynamically stable with normal oxygen saturation and no signs of shock or acute respiratory failure. Time-critical conditions like STEMI, stroke, or tension pneumothorax are not indicated by current findings.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1: AML) has posterior 0.35 which is below 0.75 threshold. Dangerous alternatives (B1.2: CML-BC with posterior 0.15, B1.1 with danger 0.9) remain unresolved and require further differentiation."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.4, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.350054020682204, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'neoplasm', 'Leukocytosis', 'leukemia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.55}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1.1", "label": "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML)", "posterior": 0.35, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.2", "B2", "B3.1"]}}, "raw_result": [{"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 35% blasts in peripheral blood with concurrent anemia and thrombocytopenia align with de novo AML's typical presentation of marrow failure and blast proliferation?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the 35% blasts in peripheral blood with concurrent anemia and thrombocytopenia align with de novo AML's typical presentation of marrow failure and blast proliferation?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the high leukocyte count (57,500/mm³) with blasts represent a chronic myeloid neoplasm in blast crisis (CML-BC), given its typical leukocytosis and transformation pattern?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the high leukocyte count (57,500/mm³) with blasts represent a chronic myeloid neoplasm in blast crisis (CML-BC), given its typical leukocytosis and transformation pattern?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of blasts and marrow failure in this patient align with MDS-EB's pathophysiology of ineffective hematopoiesis and blast accumulation?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the combination of blasts and marrow failure in this patient align with MDS-EB's pathophysiology of ineffective hematopoiesis and blast accumulation?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the high leukocyte count with blasts in a patient without prior CML history support the possibility of CML in blast crisis (B3.1)?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the high leukocyte count with blasts in a patient without prior CML history support the possibility of CML in blast crisis (B3.1)?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of bone marrow infiltration signs (e.g., hepatosplenomegaly, skin lesions) in the physical exam disfavor de novo AML as the primary diagnosis?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the absence of bone marrow infiltration signs (e.g., hepatosplenomegaly, skin lesions) in the physical exam disfavor de novo AML as the primary diagnosis?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset over days with constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) argue against CML-BC in favor of a de novo acute process?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the subacute onset over days with constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) argue against CML-BC in favor of a de novo acute process?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of abnormal mean corpuscular volume (MCV) or bone marrow morphology in the lab results disfavor MDS-EB as a diagnosis?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the absence of abnormal mean corpuscular volume (MCV) or bone marrow morphology in the lab results disfavor MDS-EB as a diagnosis?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or Ph chromosome detection in the vignette findings disfavor CML in blast crisis (B3.1)?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or Ph chromosome detection in the vignette findings disfavor CML in blast crisis (B3.1)?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) in a patient with high leukocyte count disfavor polycythemia vera (PV) as a diagnosis?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the presence of anemia (Hb 10 g/dL) in a patient with high leukocyte count disfavor polycythemia vera (PV) as a diagnosis?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the thrombocytopenia (109,000/mm³) contradict essential thrombocythemia (ET) in chronic/accelerated phase (B3.3) and support a different etiology?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the thrombocytopenia (109,000/mm³) contradict essential thrombocythemia (ET) in chronic/accelerated phase (B3.3) and support a different etiology?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}], "lr_reference": "[LR Reference for 'Hypertension' (source: HPO, RAG-context, RAG-quant:Pathology_Robbins, RAG-quant:corpus)]\n  Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: LR+=6.0, LR-=0.1176 (Sn=0.9, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: moderate increase → suggests moderate_for]\n  Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder: LR+=0.3333, LR-=1.1176 (Sn=0.05, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n  Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis: LR+=2.0, LR-=0.8235 (Sn=0.3, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: small increase → suggests weak_for]\n  De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML): [RAG context from Etiology of Acute Leukemia: A Review. > Clinical Significance]\n    \"Prognostic Assessment and Treatment Strategies...\"\n  Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC): LR+=0.0667, LR-=1.1647 (Sn=0.01, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: large/conclusive decrease → suggests strong_against]\n  Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB) / Secondary AML: LR+=4.6667, LR-=0.3529 (Sn=0.7, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: small increase → suggests weak_for]\n  Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=0.0667, LR-=1.1647 (Sn=0.01, Sp=0.85, confidence=rag_extracted) [EBM: large/conclusive decrease → suggests strong_against]\n  Polycythemia Vera (PV) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=1.79, LR-=0.21 (Sn=0.895, Sp=0.5, confidence=medium) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Essential Thrombocythemia (ET) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: [RAG context from Management of essential thrombocythemia. > Evaluation]\n    \"The World Health Organization diagnostic criteria for ET are established if all 4 major or 3 major and 1 minor criteria are met.[7]...\"\n  Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=0.3948, LR-=1.4576 (Sn=0.17, Sp=0.5694, confidence=medium) [EBM: small decrease → suggests weak_against]\n[LR Reference for 'Anemia' (source: Guideline_common, HPO, RAG-context, RAG-quant:InternalMed_Harrison, RAG-quant:corpus, clinical_supplement:Harrison)]\n  Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: LR+=1.79, LR-=0.21 (Sn=0.895, Sp=0.5, confidence=medium) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder: LR+=2.3333, LR-=0.4286 (Sn=0.7, Sp=0.7, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: small increase → suggests weak_for]\n  Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis: LR+=1.0, LR-=1.0 (Sn=0.3, Sp=0.7, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: no change → neutral]\n  De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML): LR+=1.13, LR-=0.6 (Sn=0.85, Sp=0.25, confidence=medium) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Blast Crisis (CML-BC): qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts (MDS-EB) / Secondary AML: [RAG context from Epidemiology of aplastic anemia: a study of 1324 cases. > Pathophysiology]\n    \"Aplastic anemia may progress to paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PNH), myelodysplastic syndromes (MDS), or acute myeloid leukemia (AML) due to gen...\"\n  Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Polycythemia Vera (PV) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=1.0, LR-=1.0 (Sn=0.3, Sp=0.7, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: no change → neutral]\n  Essential Thrombocythemia (ET) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=2.0, LR-=0.5714 (Sn=0.6, Sp=0.7, confidence=rag_qualitative) [EBM: small increase → suggests weak_for]\n  Primary Myelofibrosis (PMF) in Chronic/Accelerated Phase: LR+=1.09, LR-=0.91 (Sn=0.545, Sp=0.5, confidence=medium) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n[LR Reference for 'Elevated blast count' (source: