{
  "result_summary": "The presence of 35% blasts, anemia, and thrombocytopenia supports de novo AML (B1.1) but is inconsistent with chronic myeloid neoplasm phases. Absence of bone marrow infiltration signs (hepatosplenomegaly) moderately disfavors de novo AML. The high leukocyte count with blasts in a patient without prior CML history strongly disfavors CML in blast crisis (B1.2) and chronic phase CML (B3.1). Thrombocytopenia weakly disfavors essential thrombocythemia (B3.3), while anemia moderately supports polycythemia vera (B3.2) in chronic phase.",
  "per_action_effects": [
